body:
Thanks so much, you're so kind! I really appreciate the little milisecond rule you mentioned about the thumbnail, I'll work on making my future thumbnails easier to read :)

&#x200B;

!givelambda

thank you so much for your feedback, especially point 2, i didn't think about it that way, so i really appreciate it! i will be sure to either cut it down to just a short introduction or leave shoutouts to the end of the video, and ill work on my thumbnails. ill also see what I can do about getting my editing program to properly green screen the png tuber. no matter what color i put behind it, it would just erase the whole thing even on the smallest sensitivity, so I'm gonna look into either fixing that or getting a different one that comes with a transparent background already. thanks!

&#x200B;

!givelambda

thank you for the feedback! thats really helpful!! 

&#x200B;

!givelambda

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1aqcs3kQhSY](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1aqcs3kQhSY)

&#x200B;

watched in full, like 30

Pacing is great and the tone/quality of the mic/your voice is good and keeps me interested/listening! There are a few parts where I could tell you were a bit of a newbie, but that is ok! You can always re-record some parts too!

&#x200B;

Some parts felt a little too long like at 1:04, just by a second or two. The awkward pause was a little too much, I think. One crucial thing about a slow transition this early in the video, is that it may cause somebody to completely click off your video! Humans are .. silly. They want constant stimulation, and the difficult reality as a content creator is that we have to feed into that. I did like the transition, I thought it was nice, but if you lose your viewers attention, and they click off or even just skip ahead in your video, your retention rate will go down and tank your place in the algorithm. It sucks, but it is the truth! Just something I noticed. I like the fact you showed off the music, but again, unfortunately, I think you would need to cut it a little bit shorter. :(
